      "writtenOn": "2021-10-01T18:51:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure how to set color_2 and color_3 values in this Macro as I need to set those only if color_2 and color_3 nodes exist.\n\nOption 1:\nif (DT_NODE_EXISTS(DT_CHILD(id, color_2))) {\n    led_values[CHARGE_STATE(id)][CHIPSET_STATE(id)].color_2 \u003d \n            COLOR(id, color_2);\n} -\u003e This still tries to look for color_2 child node for each node ID, so the build fails\n\nOption 2:\n#if (DT_NODE_EXISTS(DT_CHILD(id, color_2))\n    led_values[CHARGE_STATE(id)][CHIPSET_STATE(id)].color_2 \u003d \n            COLOR(id, color_2);\n#endif -\u003e This still fails as it is not allowing #ifdefs within macro.\n\nOption 3: \nCODE_COND_1(DT_NODE_EXISTS(DT_CHILD(id, color_2), \n            led_values[CHARGE_STATE(id)][CHIPSET_STATE(id)].color_2 \u003d \n            COLOR(id, color_2), \n            ())\n-\u003e The build for this also fails",
      "revId": "12cd65e02f573309be2ebe31abc82e6b95c78efc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
